<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<object-views xmlns="http://axelor.com/xml/ns/object-views"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://axelor.com/xml/ns/object-views
    http://axelor.com/xml/ns/object-views/object-views_7.4.xsd">

  <!-- NEUTRALISED EXTENSION — it exists only so that a restore replaces what used to be here.

    This file used to add a "Address map / Nominatim" panel to the stock Preferences dialog plus an
    onLoad/onSave pair calling BgNominatimPreferencesController, so an admin could edit the shared
    AppBgLocalization.nominatimUserAgent value. That never saved reliably, and because the onSave
    hook ran on EVERY save of the dialog it could refuse ordinary preference changes (language,
    theme, password) that have nothing to do with geocoding. The setting itself is gone: the
    Nominatim User-Agent is now a compile-time constant in NominatimHttpClientImpl.

    WHY THE FILE STAYS INSTEAD OF BEING DELETED. The form name and the extension id are unchanged,
    so "Restore all views" REPLACES the stored extension row with this harmless one. Deleting the
    file would instead rely on Axelor removing a MetaView whose source XML has vanished, which is
    not something to bet a blocked Preferences dialog on.

    WHY NOTHING TOUCHES onLoad/onSave. The computed view is rebuilt from the base view plus every
    current extension, so simply not contributing the attributes is what removes them — nothing here
    has to clear anything. Writing onLoad="" / onSave="" would be worse than useless: those are the
    STOCK form's attributes, shared by every module, and an extension that blanks them could silently
    drop an action another module contributes now or later. This extension therefore modifies no
    attribute of the stock form at all.

    WHY AN EMPTY HIDDEN PANEL. The schema requires an extension form to carry at least one <extend>,
    and <extend> requires at least one of insert/replace/move/attribute. An insert of a hidden panel
    with no fields and no actions is the smallest thing that is legal and does nothing: it renders
    nothing, reads nothing and calls nothing. The old panel and its two actions are simply gone. -->
  <form name="user-preferences-form" title="Preferences" id="bg-localization-user-preferences-form"
    model="com.axelor.auth.db.User" extension="true">
    <extend target="//panel[@title='User preferences']">
      <insert position="after">
        <panel name="bgNominatimPreferencesPanel" hidden="true"/>
      </insert>
    </extend>
  </form>

</object-views>
